CORE
namespace.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ sizes: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.mem.class]/1, [temp.inst]/3; see test.desc.  A member class of
a class template in a namespace, depending on the template parameter, for
two instances created before its definition and one after it.  The
definition is written inside the namespace: the qualified form `struct
ns::S<C>::N { ... };' is not grafted at all yet (also for instances created
later).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
